The O16 verdict said "THESIS FAILS ON THIS CARRIER — chiral reversal is NOT
total". True as far as it went, and misleading: §4b measures that chiral
succeeds on EXACTLY the 2752 triples forward succeeds on (set equality), so
the inversion costs nothing — what fails at the octonion loop is the FORWARD
law itself, and its shortfall is exactly the associator.

The same section shows why the count alone could not decide it: on O16 bare
and forward have the SAME COUNT (2752 each) and DIFFERENT SETS, intersecting
in 1408 = 16 x 88 = |S| x commuting-pairs. A count-only test would have called
bare and chiral equivalent there.

Verdicts now carry chiral_co_extensive_with_forward /
bare_co_extensive_with_forward / forward_and_bare_intersection, and the O16
row reads REVERSAL IS NOT REWIND, CONDITIONALLY.

